From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 10:44:07 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Read the light values through one chunk lookup

getLightFor asked isLoaded whether the chunk was there and then
getChunkAtWorldCoords for the chunk itself - two probes of the same map
under the same key. Once a chunk is loaded getOrCreateChunk returns
exactly what getChunkIfLoaded already found, so the second probe is
redundant.

With Chunk.getBrightness and Chunk.canSeeSky now taking coordinates, the
scratch position goes with it, and the BlockPosition form of getLightFor
no longer allocates a replacement position for negative y - it just
delegates.

This is the hottest read in the light flood fill: c() visits up to 32768
cells, probing six neighbours each, and getRawLight adds another six
reads per cell on top.

setLightFor gets the same treatment. It keeps its scratch position
because notifyLightSet passes one to the world accesses.

What this drops is getOrCreateChunk's "chunk stored at the wrong
coordinates" error log on the light path. It only fires on an already
corrupt chunk map, and every other caller of getOrCreateChunk in the
same tick still reports it.

The assumption these two rest on is about ChunkProviderServer's map, not
about anything a unit test can reach, so debugVerifyAthenaIndexes now
also checks on every light query that the reused chunk is the one the
provider would have handed back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

